  },
  {
    label: 'Communication as a multiplier skill',
    body: 'A technically strong person who explains their work clearly gets picked for visible projects far more often than an equally strong person who does not.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Market positioning - being findable and legible',
    body: 'A LinkedIn profile, a small public portfolio, or a simple write-up of what you have built makes you discoverable for opportunities you never formally applied to.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Personal fit over copying someone else\'s path',
    body: 'The best skill to build alongside your job is the one that matches your working style and interests closely enough that you will actually keep going after a tiring week at work.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Financial reality of the time you invest',
    body: 'Skill-building alongside a first job should fit inside real evenings and weekends, not a fantasy schedule - a smaller, consistent effort beats an ambitious plan you abandon in six weeks.',
