  },
  {
    q: 'Is campus placement enough, or do I also need to apply off-campus?',
    a: 'Campus placement alone is rarely enough unless your college draws a large, high-quality set of visiting companies. The number of recruiters visiting a campus tracks the college\'s brand and location closely, so students at colleges with thinner placement drives need off-campus portals and referrals as a genuine second lane, not a backup plan.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I ask for a referral if I do not know anyone at the company?',
    a: 'Search LinkedIn for alumni from your college or past interns at the company, and message them with one specific piece of proof of your work plus the exact role you are targeting. Ask for one small, specific thing, such as forwarding your resume, rather than a vague request for help. A weak connection who replies is worth more than a strong connection you never message.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should I use Naukri, LinkedIn, or Indeed for my first job search in India?',
    a: 'Use more than one. Each portal indexes different roles and different employer relationships, and none of them covers every opening. Add the government-run National Career Service to the mix for free listings and apprenticeship options that commercial portals do not always carry.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What should I focus on in my early days once I get my first job?',
    a: 'Most Indian employers set a formal review window in the early months of a new hire\'s time with the company, so treat that stretch as a chance to build visible proof: understand what your manager actually measures, ship one small, complete piece of work early, and ask specific questions instead of guessing. The habits you build in this window tend to set the pattern for how the rest of the role goes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'I have been rejected from every application so far. What should I change?',
    a: 'First check whether your resume is matched closely enough to the listed skills in each posting to clear an automated screen; a generic resume applied broadly usually explains a long silent streak better than a lack of ability does. Second, check whether referrals are part of your weekly effort at all, since that channel converts at clearly higher rates than cold applications in large employer datasets.',
  },
