  <p>
    Applying is only half the work - the other half is choosing the right lanes, comparing offers on more than the starting number, and building a skill portfolio alongside the job once you are in it. <strong>That combination, not the job title alone, is what unlocks earlier financial freedom and better opportunities over the next few years.</strong> If you want a search and skill-building plan built around your actual degree, city, and target companies instead of generic advice, <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">structured career guidance</a> can help you build it.
